.TH WAYBAR-SYSMON 1 "2026-09-23" "system-monitor-sway" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
waybar-sysmon \- stacked CPU/memory/network graphs as a native Waybar module
.SH SYNOPSIS
Load
.I /usr/lib/system-monitor-sway/waybar_sysmon.so
as a
.I cffi/sysmon
module in the Waybar config.
.SH DESCRIPTION
system-monitor-sway draws GNOME system-monitor style stacked area charts
directly inside
.BR Waybar
via its CFFI plugin API: no overlay window, no image file, no scripting
runtime. Placement, fullscreen behavior and stacking belong to Waybar and
Sway, so graphs are covered by fullscreen windows automatically.
.PP
First cut: cpu, memory and net graphs only, with labels but no tooltips.
.SS Waybar configuration
Merge
.I /usr/share/system-monitor-sway/waybar-config-example.jsonc
into
.IR ~/.config/waybar/config.json :
.EX
"modules-center": ["cffi/sysmon"],
"cffi/sysmon": {
  "module_path": "/usr/lib/system-monitor-sway/waybar_sysmon.so",
  "graph_width": 100,
  "height": 30,
  "spacing": 4,
  "interval_ms": 1000,
  "background": "#ffffff16",
  "graphs": ["cpu", "memory", "net"]
}
.EE
All keys after
.I module_path
are optional; defaults are shown. graphs selects a subset in canonical
order. Labels default to cpu, mem and net
.RI ( show_label ,
.IR label_cpu ,
.IR label_memory ,
.IR label_net ;
set
.I show_label
to false to hide them). Labels render vertically (bottom-to-top) in a
14 px slot; text longer than the bar height is truncated. Refresh periods default to cpu 1500 ms, memory 5000 ms, net
1000 ms (minimum 250 ms) via
.IR refresh_cpu_ms ,
.IR refresh_memory_ms ,
.IR refresh_net_ms .
Chart colors default to the GNOME applet palette and can be overridden
with
.IR colors_cpu ,
.IR colors_memory ,
.IR colors_net
(arrays of exactly 5 / 3 / 5
.IR #rrggbb
entries; a wrong-sized array keeps the defaults).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYBAR_SYSMON_DEBUG
If set, log sampling, paint and lifecycle diagnostics to Waybar's stderr.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/system-monitor-sway/waybar_sysmon.so
The module (path varies with install PREFIX).
.TP
.I /usr/share/system-monitor-sway/waybar-config-example.jsonc
Annotated config example.
.SH NOTES
The module targets Waybar's CFFI ABI v2. If Waybar ever requires a newer
ABI, the module refuses to load with an error instead of misrendering.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (1),
.BR swaymsg (1),
.BR waybar (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jerome Berclaz.
